InitCondFile                       binary_ics
OutputDir                          output

% e=0.9, q=0.1, a=100 AU, M=1.1 Msun -> P_orb = 9.751362e-04 code time.
%
% 1000 orbits. 64 was enough to see a drift but not to pin its growth law: over that range
% |da/a| spans less than a decade and the fitted exponent came out t^+1.42, which the longer
% baseline shows was noise (it settles to t^+0.94). At 1000 orbits both diagnostics span more
% than three decades and the exponents are firm -- COM drift t^+0.991, i.e. linear to 1%,
% which is what separates a secular leak from the t^0.5 of a random walk.
%
% Costs ~3 min of GIZMO, serial. Snapshots every P/4 rather than P/8: that is still four per
% orbit, enough for the per-orbit envelope, and halves the file count. 4000 files at 16 KB is
% ~65 MB and 4000 inodes, which matters on a quota'd home filesystem.
TimeMax                            9.751362e-01
TimeBetSnapshot                    2.437840e-04
TimeOfFirstSnapshot                0
TimeBegin                          0
TimeBetStatistics                  2.437840e-04
BoxSize                            1

% MaxSizeTimestep = P/20, so apocentre is resolved even where the accuracy criterion would
% happily take a longer step. MinSizeTimestep must clear pericentre: (1-e)^1.5 = 0.032 of the
% mean motion, and the accuracy criterion asks for far less than that again, so leave it tiny.
MaxSizeTimestep                    4.875681e-05
MinSizeTimestep                    1e-14
ErrTolIntAccuracy                  0.005
ErrTolTheta                        0.5
ErrTolForceAcc                     0.0025
CourantFac                         0.4
MaxRMSDisplacementFac              0.125
TreeDomainUpdateFrequency          0.1
DesNumNgb                          32
MaxNumNgbDeviation                 1
MaxMemSize                         2000
PartAllocFactor                    2.5
BufferSize                         100
ResubmitOn                         0
ResubmitCommand                    none
UnitLength_in_cm                   3.085678e+18
UnitMass_in_g                      1.989e+33
UnitVelocity_in_cm_per_s           100000

% Pericentre is 4.848e-5 pc. Softening is set 500x below that so the force is Newtonian over
% the whole orbit and the test measures the INTEGRATOR, not the kernel. (The production
% STARFORGE value, 3.117e-5, would be comparable to pericentre here and would dominate.)
Softening_Type0                    1e-7
Softening_Type1                    1e-7
Softening_Type2                    1e-7
Softening_Type3                    1e-7
Softening_Type4                    1e-7
Softening_Type5                    1e-7
Softening_Type0_MaxPhysLimit       1e-7
Softening_Type1_MaxPhysLimit       1e-7
Softening_Type2_MaxPhysLimit       1e-7
Softening_Type3_MaxPhysLimit       1e-7
Softening_Type4_MaxPhysLimit       1e-7
Softening_Type5_MaxPhysLimit       1e-7
AGS_DesNumNgb                      32
AGS_MaxNumNgbDeviation             1
CritPhysDensity                    1e13
CpuTimeBetRestartFile              30

% No gas in this test, so the default multi-pc accretion search is pure tree-walk overhead.
SinkMaxAccretionRadius             1e-6
